                            305FIX.EXE
   
   305FIX.EXE is a small file that will patch FALCON3.EXE or 
   FALCONCD.EXE to eliminate the "Cannot Create File" error 
   when playing multi-player comms in Falcon.  It should (and 
   can) be applied to version 3.05 only.
   
   THIS PROGRAM ALTERS THE FALCON 3.05 EXECUTABLE FILE;  BACK 
   UP FALCON3.EXE/FALCONCD.EXE BEFORE RUNNING THIS PROGRAM.
   
   To use it, simply copy the file 305FIX.EXE into your Falcon 
   directory and type "305FIX <Enter>."  
   
   After this, and before starting Falcon, do the following 
   from the DOS prompt:
   
   Type "ATTRIB -H SQUAD6.MTV"; press <Enter>.
   Type "DEL SQUAD6.*"; press <Enter>.
   
   For maximum safety, all systems involved (caller and 
   answerers) should apply this patch and follow the above 
   steps.
   
   Now, the warnings:
   
   There are no guarantees, warrantees, promises, assurances, 
   or even encouraging words (of any kind!) associated with the 
   use of this program.  It changes two bytes in the Falcon exe 
   file and so forces it to create SQUAD6.MTV with a clear 
   attribute byte instead of the erroneous one where the hidden 
   bit was set.  I personally can see no way this could cause 
   other trouble, and its use has cleared up the problem on my 
   system.
   
   This patch is in no way endorsed by Spectrum Holobyte.
   
   Distribution:
   
   This file may be freely distributed as long as this document 
   is included, unaltered, with 305FIX.EXE.
   
   That's the end of the required reading, but you might be 
   interested in what's below.
   
   Unsolicited Advertisement:
   
   (This patch is free--you can read an ad!) This file was 
   written because I'm adding some new comms features to
   my Strategic Falcon program and this bug was getting in the 
   way.  What is Strategic Falcon?  I'm glad you asked!  
   Strategic Falcon is a campaign enhancement to Falcon 3.0.  
   Here's what it does:
   
   Tactical Features
   
   Fly any allied aircraft in Falcon 3.0!  Version 1.2 of 
   StratFalc allows you to change the type of aircraft *you* 
   fly--you can pilot, for example, A-10s for CAS runs, F-4s 
   for SEAD, or B-52s for bombing!  Although the cockpit will 
   still look like an F-16, all external views of the aircraft 
   and, especially, the aircraft's flight model will be that of 
   the new plane!
   
   Add, remove, or alter F-16 flights, much like in Falcon 3.0 
   itself, with some important additions:  Fuel remaining and 
   Time to Waypoint are always displayed.
   
   Change the location of F-16 starting and ending waypoints 
   (these are normally "locked" in Falcon itself).
   
   Add, remove, or alter Allied or Enemy flights.
   
   Change the types of aircraft for any flight in this mission. 
   (Although your "personal plane" must always be an F-16.)
   
   Change the waypoints of any flight--F-16, allied, or enemy--
   involved in a mission.
   
   Change the temperament and skill levels of any allied or 
   enemy pilot.
   
   Change the weapon loadout of any aircraft involved.
   
   Add or remove ground paths and ground units.
   
   Change the types, waypoints, and temperament of any ground 
   units.
   
   Make ground columns more realistic;  no more "kill me fast" 
   in-line formations.
   
   Limit the number of killer SA-7s you face.
   
   View the mission description with the press of a key.
   
   Check mission timing with the "synchronized timing trace" 
   feature, which shows with graphical/animated symbols where 
   each flight in the mission will be in relation to each 
   other!
   
   Swap your F-16 flight waypoints with those of any other F-16 
   flight--useful when you don't want to fly the lead mission.
   
   Load every plane correctly and automatically--up to 18 
   preset loadouts for each plane type!
   
   
   Strategic Features
   
   Change the occupation of any site, to instantly capture 
   nodes or surrender them to the enemy.
   
   Change the current strength or capacity of any site.
   
   Change the rate of growth of any site.
   
   Change the quantity of specific unit types at a site (the 
   site's "breakdown").
   
   Change the node structure for the theater.  You can cut any 
   site off from resupply.
   
   Change which nodes mean victory and which spell defeat.
   
   You can even fully randomize victory/defeat sites!
   
   Launch an automatic, coordinated ground attack against any 
   site.
   
   Simulation Mode changes the way you play Falcon!  Aircraft 
   squadrons are assigned to bases--you can transfer at will--
   but your resources are limited!  Three brigades await your 
   orders, but if you screw up, they pay!
   
   Other Features
   
   Change the current weather and the altitude of the cloud 
   cover.  Also change the predicted weather.
   
   Change the home air base--you can fly a campaign from any 
   allied-occupied strip.
   
   Place an ILS at any base.
   
   Change the current day and time.
   
   Change the resupply and replacement days and times.
   
   Change the campaign momentum, both macro and micro--turn the 
   tide on the enemy.
   
   Learn to properly use the "Kill Boxes" which have always 
   been present in Falcon 3.0.
   
   If you wish, all enemy-related information can be hidden 
   from you by checking a single box.
   
   Run Falcon or any series of programs with the press of a key 
   and automatically return to StratFalc when you're done.
   
   
   System Requirements: 
   
   The program is entirely graphical;  to use it you *must* 
   have a mouse.  It also requires Falcon 3.0, any version from 
   3.01.1 through 3.05.
   
   
